# Core Production Standards

- Use `Next.js` with **App Router** only (`src/app`).
- Keep `TypeScript` in **strict mode**; do not bypass with `any` sem justificativa forte.
- Prefer component-based architecture with reusable primitives in `src/components`.
- Style with `TailwindCSS`; avoid scattered inline styles except tiny dynamic cases.
- Build mobile-first layouts and expand to tablet/desktop via breakpoints.
- Keep UI blocks composable and reusable across pages.
- Deliver production-ready code: typed, testable, maintainable, and readable.

## Quick Example

```tsx
// ✅ good: reusable typed component
type SectionProps = { title: string; children: React.ReactNode };
export function Section({ title, children }: SectionProps) {
  return <section className="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">{children}</section>;
}
```
